CORE
main.cpp
--cpp98
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ friend may convert to private base: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
FAILURE
--
N5008 [class.access.base]/4-5: derived-to-private-base conversion is
accessible in a FRIEND of the derived class.  Was judged only from the
constructor's own class scope at reference-binding time, so the
conversion was rejected ("no match") and, in libstdc++'s _Hashtable,
the befriended _Insert mixin's member body was silently dropped
(unordered_set::insert was a no-op).  Header-free.
